--- Finding (multiple_distinct_objects): a collecting `for` over `range[n]`, where n
--- can fail (`int['3']`), whose body adds the loop's int to a growing int, is an
--- internal error interpreted and does not build compiled.
---
--- crow run -i:  runtime error: line 22: internal error: an int met a float in 'add'
---               without a conversion — a bug in Crow, not in this program
--- crow run:     error[E0277]: the trait bound `Vec<i64>: FromParallelIterator<f64>`
---               is not satisfied (the sum is typed as a float), and with `i + n`
---               in place of `i + 3 ^ 40`: error[E0277]: cannot add
---               `crow_runtime::int::Int` to `i64`
---               error: the compiled program does not build — …
--- Expected: [12157665459056928801, 12157665459056928802, 12157665459056928803]
--- in both modes (what `range[3]` in place of `range[n]` prints in both).
---
--- Each of these runs and agrees: `range[3]`; `m = 3` / `range[m]`; `big = 3 ^ 40`
--- with `range[3]`; `i + 1` (no growing int); a statement loop
--- (`for i in range[n]` / `log[i + n]`). Related: findings/multiple_distinct_objects-1.co
--- (the same item handed to a function taking a growing int) and the known
--- findings/french_republican_calendar-1.co (the item compared with one).
n = int['3']
ds = for i in range[n]
    i + 3 ^ 40
log[ds]
